Package: command
Type: Package
Title: Process Command Line Arguments
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "John",
           family = "Bryant",
	   email = "john@bayesiandemography.com",
	   role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Bayesian Demography Limited",
            role = "cph"))
Description: Process command line arguments. Processing includes
    checking arguments, matching arguments to names,
    and automatically converting strings to numbers, logical values,
    or dates. The main function, `cmd_assign()`, is designed to be
    used a part of an automated workflow, but can also be used interactively
    for development and testing. The aim is give files well-defined interfaces,
    with clear inputs and outputs.
